## 4. Technical Architecture

### 4.1 Frontend Architecture (Flutter)
```
lib/
├── core/
│   ├── router/          # App navigation and routing
│   ├── services/        # API services, auth service
│   ├── theme/           # App theming and colors
│   ├── utils/           # Helper functions
│   └── widgets/         # Reusable UI components
├── data/
│   ├── models/          # Data models
│   └── mock/            # Mock data for development
└── features/
    ├── employee/        # Employee-specific features
    │   ├── data/
    │   ├── domain/
    │   └── presentation/
    ├── manager/         # Manager-specific features
    │   ├── data/
    │   ├── domain/
    │   └── presentation/
    └── admin/           # Admin-specific features
        ├── data/
        ├── domain/
        └── presentation/
```

### 4.2 Backend Architecture (Flask)
```
backend/
├── app/
│   ├── models/          # Database models
│   ├── routes/          # API endpoints
│   │   ├── auth.py
│   │   ├── employee.py
│   │   ├── manager.py
│   │   └── admin.py
│   ├── services/        # Business logic
│   ├── utils/           # Helper functions
│   └── middleware/      # Auth, CORS, etc.
├── config/              # Configuration files
├── migrations/          # Database migrations
└── tests/               # Unit and integration tests
```

### 4.3 Database Schema

#### Users Table
```sql
- id (Primary Key)
- email (Unique)
- password_hash
- full_name
- phone
- role (Employee/Manager/Admin)
- department_id (Foreign Key)
- manager_id (Foreign Key to Users)
- profile_photo_url
- is_active
- created_at
- updated_at
```

#### Departments Table
```sql
- id (Primary Key)
- name
- manager_id (Foreign Key to Users)
- description
- location
- created_at
- updated_at
```

#### Attendance Table
```sql
- id (Primary Key)
- user_id (Foreign Key)
- check_in_time
- check_in_location (Lat, Long)
- check_out_time
- check_out_location (Lat, Long)
- total_hours
- status (Present/Absent/Half Day)
- date
- notes
- created_at
- updated_at
```

#### Leaves Table
```sql
- id (Primary Key)
- user_id (Foreign Key)
- leave_type (Sick/Casual/Annual)
- start_date
- end_date
- total_days
- reason
- status (Pending/Approved/Rejected)
- approved_by (Foreign Key to Users)
- approval_date
- manager_comments
- attachment_url
- created_at
- updated_at
```

#### Holidays Table
```sql
- id (Primary Key)
- name
- date
- is_optional
- department_id (NULL for company-wide)
- description
- created_at
- updated_at
```

