## 8. Security & Authentication

### 8.1 Authentication Flow
1. User login with email/password
2. Backend validates credentials
3. JWT token generated with 24-hour expiration
4. Token stored in secure storage (Flutter Secure Storage)
5. Token included in all API requests (Authorization header)
6. Token refresh mechanism for extended sessions

### 8.2 Authorization
- **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
- Route guards based on user roles
- API endpoint permissions
- Data filtering based on user scope

### 8.3 Data Security
- Password hashing (bcrypt)
- HTTPS for all communications
- SQL injection prevention
- XSS protection
- CSRF tokens
- Rate limiting
- Input validation and sanitization

### 8.4 Privacy
- GDPR compliance
- Data retention policies
- User consent management
- Right to be forgotten
- Data export capabilities

---

## 9. Performance Requirements

### 9.1 Response Times
- Page load: < 2 seconds
- API responses: < 500ms
- Real-time updates: < 1 second

### 9.2 Scalability
- Support 10,000+ users
- Concurrent users: 1,000+
- Database optimization with indexing
- Caching strategies (Redis)

### 9.3 Availability
- 99.9% uptime
- Load balancing
- Backup systems
- Disaster recovery plan

